/* book exam traps: AM's FOM is at most 1/3, not 1. At m = 1, FOM = 1/3 (−4.77 dB); only coherent DSB-SC and SSB reach 1. | (3/2)β² is not free: the bandwidth is 2(β + 1)W, and the formula fails below the FM threshold. | Do not mix conventions. (3/2)β² uses input noise in W; with input noise in BT = 2(β + 1)W the same receiver has FOM = 3β²(β + 1). | In dB, add: (S/N)o (dB) = (S/N)c (dB) + 10 log FOM. Never add a ratio to a dB value. | The FM output noise rises as f² in power, a triangle in amplitude. It is the noise that rises, not the signal. */
