/* book: lead: FM gives its large noise improvement only while the received carrier is well above the noise. When the carrier-to-noise ratio in the IF bandwidth falls to about 10 dB, the output starts to crackle with clicks and the output SNR drops far faster than the ideal law. This is the threshold effect. The same nonlinear behaviour of the limiter and discriminator gives the capture effect: of two FM signals */
/* book Figure 3.6.1: The two receivers of the worked examples. Above threshold each line rises 1 dB for 1 dB of carrier power, β = 5 sitting higher; but β = 5 needs −111.4 dBm to reach threshold and β = 2 only −114.4 dBm, so the narrower system keeps working on weaker signals. */
