/* book Worked example: Q: An FM broadcast receiver has an IF bandwidth BT = 180 kHz (β = 5, W = 15 kHz) and receives noise N0 = kT0 = 4 × 10⁻²¹ W/Hz. Taking the threshold as ρ = 10 dB, find the noise power, the carrier power at threshold, and the output SNR there.
   1. N = N0BT = 4 × 10⁻²¹ × 1.8 × 10⁵ = 7.2 × 10⁻¹⁶ W = 10 log(7.2 × 10⁻¹³) = −121.4 dBm.
   2. At ρ = 10 dB: C = 10 × 7.2 × 10⁻¹⁶ = 7.2 × 10⁻¹⁵ W = −111.4 dBm.
   3. Improvement 3β²(β + 1) = 3 × 25 × 6 = 450 = 26.5 dB.
   4. Output SNR at threshold = 10 + 26.5 = 36.5 dB. In channel-SNR terms, (S/N)c = 12ρ = 120 = 20.8 dB, and 20.8 + 15.7 (the FOM in dB) gives the same 36.5 dB.
   Answer: N = 7.2 × 10⁻¹⁶ W (−121.4 dBm); C at threshold = 7.2 × 10⁻¹⁵ W (−111.4 dBm); output SNR there 36.5 dB. */
