/* book exam traps: The threshold is a carrier-to-noise ratio of about 10 dB in the IF bandwidth; do not quote it as an output SNR or as a fixed power in watts. | Below threshold the straight-line law does not hold; do not use (S/N)o = 3β²(β + 1)ρ there. | Capture ratio is not threshold. Capture compares two signal powers; threshold compares carrier with noise. | A larger β improves the output above threshold but raises the carrier power needed to reach threshold (worked example 2). | Keep the two SNR measures apart: ρ uses the noise in BT, the channel SNR uses the noise in W; they differ by BT/W = 2(β + 1). */
